# A read of a key that only a pattern constraint matches. Only a field with a
# predictable name is declared (docs/translation.md, A4), so a lens reads no
# key under a pattern, beneath it or in a condition; it copies labels whole.
-- source.cue --
labels: [string]: {v: string}
-- target.cue --
tags: [string]: {v: string}
env?: string
deep?: string
-- lens.cue --
v0_0: _
v1_0: {
	tags: v0_0.labels
	env:  v0_0.labels.env.v
	if v0_0.labels.prod != _|_ {deep: "prod"}
}
-- out --
not total
v1_0 is under the pattern v0_0.labels.prod != _|_, but the source schema does not declare v0_0.labels.prod: only a pattern constraint matches it (rule source-undeclared) @ lens.cue:5:2
  help: a lens reads only fields declared by name: declare labels.prod as an optional field in a new minor version of the source schema, for the values instances carry there to land in, then map from it in the lens from that version
v1_0.env copies v0_0.labels.env.v, which the source schema does not declare: only a pattern constraint matches v0_0.labels.env (rule source-undeclared) @ lens.cue:4:8
